-- Ronald Isley: a fuller brand story. Idempotent; only replaces the original short seed copy, so a story edited in the admin is left alone.
update brands set story = E'For more than six decades, Ronald Isley has defined excellence in music, style, and culture. His unmistakable voice, timeless hits, and influence on generations have made him a true icon.\n\nBorn in Cincinnati, Ohio, on May 21, 1941, Ronald is the lead voice and a founding member of The Isley Brothers. The group''s debut single, “Shout,” arrived in 1959, and over the decades his smooth tenor carried soul, funk and R&B through the T-Neck Records years and the landmark 3 + 3 album of 1973.\n\nThe honors followed. The Isley Brothers entered the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 1992. He joined Rod Stewart on a top-ten version of “This Old Heart of Mine” in 1990, teamed up with Burt Bacharach on Here I Am in 2003, and stepped out on his own in 2010 with his first solo album, Mr. I. In 2016, Berklee College of Music awarded him an honorary doctorate of music.\n\nThe Plug cigar is an extension of that legacy. A smooth, refined smoke for those who appreciate the finer things in life and move with purpose.'
where slug = 'ronald-isley' and story like 'For more than six decades%' and story not like '%Cincinnati%';
